WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
Follow the timeout sequence.
The provider accepts

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.560
the transfer and the journal commits,
but the response is lost.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.360
The client cannot infer
failure from the timeout.

00:00:09.573 --> 00:00:14.000
It retries with the same key and payload,
and the service resolves the original

00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:17.920
transfer without posting again.
The test checks identity,

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:22.400
journal count and balances.
Run a duplicate-posting variant as well:

00:00:22.427 --> 00:00:25.280
those same assertions must fail
when the defect is present.
